
<!-- BEGIN FM-LIVE-PROBE test-driven-development (temporary) -->
## Temporary live-observation rule

New Python test methods must start with `test_probe_`. Include `# Arrange`,
`# Act` and `# Assert` comments in each new test body.
For new behavior, run the test before changing implementation code and observe
failure specifically because the expected behavior is missing. Then show the
implementation change and a passing run. Environment, import and syntax errors
are not valid RED evidence.
<!-- END FM-LIVE-PROBE test-driven-development (temporary) -->
